{"version":2,"slug":"british-time-expressions-you-need-every-day","videoId":"BCDXweG6CLc","videoUrl":"https://youtu.be/BCDXweG6CLc","lang":"en","title":"British Time Expressions You Need Every Day ⏰","category":"Travelling","channel":"English by Jay - Sprout","channelUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/@englishbyjay.official","captionSource":"auto","tags":["Slow english","simple english learn"],"backUrl":"/","lines":[{"start":0,"text":"In England,"},{"start":1,"text":"we don't say"},{"start":390,"text":"."},{"start":390.6,"text":"We say"},{"start":391.2,"text":"half six."},{"start":391.8,"text":"We don't say"},{"start":392.4,"text":"wait a minute. We say"},{"start":393,"text":"one sec."},{"start":393.6,"text":"In this video, I will teach you"},{"start":394.2,"text":"everything you need to know"},{"start":394.8,"text":"about time."},{"start":395.4,"text":"What other ways can we say what time is"},{"start":396,"text":"it?"},{"start":396.6,"text":"Well,"},{"start":397.2,"text":"it depends on the situation."},{"start":397.8,"text":"For example, if you're at work, you"},{"start":398.4,"text":"might say"},{"start":399,"text":"Luigi, do you know what time it is?"},{"start":399.6,"text":"If you're asking a stranger in the"},{"start":400.2,"text":"streets, you would say"},{"start":400.8,"text":"Excuse me, have you got the time?"},{"start":401.4,"text":"And if you're asking a close friend or a"},{"start":402,"text":"family member, you might say"},{"start":402.6,"text":"What time is it?"},{"start":403.2,"text":"Or"},{"start":403.8,"text":"Got the time?"},{"start":404.4,"text":"It's"},{"start":420,"text":"."},{"start":420.6,"text":"Or you say"},{"start":421.2,"text":"Actually,"},{"start":421.8,"text":"it's more natural to just say it's"},{"start":422.4,"text":"."},{"start":423,"text":"And at"},{"start":423.6,"text":","},{"start":424.2,"text":"I like to"},{"start":424.8,"text":"do the horse stance for 5 minutes,"},{"start":425.4,"text":"read a book for 5 minutes,"},{"start":426,"text":"and finally,"},{"start":426.6,"text":"meditate"},{"start":427.2,"text":"for 5 minutes."},{"start":427.8,"text":"Oh, look."},{"start":428.4,"text":"It's"},{"start":435,"text":"."},{"start":435.6,"text":"Or as British people say, quarter past"},{"start":436.2,"text":"seven."},{"start":436.8,"text":"Now, I'm going to show you a simple way"},{"start":437.4,"text":"how to tell the time in Britain."},{"start":438,"text":"On the right of the clock, we say past."},{"start":438.6,"text":"On the left of the clock, we say to."},{"start":439.2,"text":"Halfway round, we say half."},{"start":439.8,"text":"And by the way, these are called hands."},{"start":440.4,"text":"Big hand, little hand."},{"start":441,"text":"So,"},{"start":441.6,"text":"right now,"},{"start":442.2,"text":"it is"},{"start":442.8,"text":"."},{"start":443.4,"text":"Now, it's"},{"start":607,"text":"."},{"start":607.6,"text":"1/4"},{"start":608.2,"text":"15 minutes later,"},{"start":608.8,"text":"it is 1/2"},{"start":609.4,"text":". 15 minutes later,"},{"start":610,"text":"it is 1/4 to"},{"start":610.6,"text":". And remember, on the"},{"start":611.2,"text":"left side of the clock, it's to, so it's"},{"start":611.8,"text":"15 minutes to"},{"start":612.4,"text":". It's 1/4 to"},{"start":613,"text":"."},{"start":613.6,"text":"Now, it's"},{"start":614.2,"text":"to"},{"start":614.8,"text":"."},{"start":615.4,"text":"to"},{"start":616,"text":"."},{"start":616.6,"text":"And"},{"start":617.2,"text":"."},{"start":617.8,"text":"Morning."},{"start":618.4,"text":"In real life conversation, it's more"},{"start":619,"text":"common to hear British people saying"},{"start":619.6,"text":"\"Morning.\" instead of good morning."},{"start":620.2,"text":"Morning is"},{"start":620.8,"text":"less formal"},{"start":621.4,"text":"and more friendly."},{"start":622,"text":"Now,"},{"start":622.6,"text":"what am I having for breaky?"},{"start":623.2,"text":"And breaky is slang for breakfast."},{"start":623.8,"text":"Mhm."},{"start":624.4,"text":"For breaky, I'm having a croissant with"},{"start":625,"text":"mulberry jam and butter."},{"start":625.6,"text":"I'm having an oat milk latte in a mug"},{"start":626.2,"text":"with a little biscuits on the saucer."},{"start":626.8,"text":"There is also a silver teaspoon."},{"start":627.4,"text":"I'm grabbing the handle"},{"start":628,"text":"and picking it up."},{"start":628.6,"text":"Now, I'm taking a sip of my latte."},{"start":629.2,"text":"Jay, have you got the time?"},{"start":629.8,"text":"Mhm."},{"start":630.4,"text":"It's 1/2"},{"start":631,"text":"."},{"start":631.6,"text":"And at"},{"start":632.2,"text":"["},{"start":632.8,"text":"I love"},{"start":633.4,"text":"to write."},{"start":634,"text":"They say that writing helps you think"},{"start":634.6,"text":"clearly."},{"start":635.2,"text":"I like to write in the morning as a nice"},{"start":635.8,"text":"and gentle way to start the day."},{"start":636.4,"text":"I usually free write."},{"start":637,"text":"And today I'm going to write about my"},{"start":637.6,"text":"environment."},{"start":638.2,"text":"I'm surrounded by greenery."},{"start":638.8,"text":"The trees are covered by plants and the"},{"start":639.4,"text":"air smells fresh."},{"start":640,"text":"I can hear the sound of chimes tinkling"},{"start":640.6,"text":"in the wind."},{"start":641.2,"text":"The sun is lighting up the pond."},{"start":641.8,"text":"The frog is cooling in the shade."},{"start":642.4,"text":"I feel happy to be in this moment."},{"start":643,"text":"Now, I think it's time"},{"start":643.6,"text":"for"},{"start":644.2,"text":"croissant."},{"start":644.8,"text":"Oh, look."},{"start":645.4,"text":"It's quarter to nine."},{"start":646,"text":"So, once I have cleared my mind, once"},{"start":646.6,"text":"I've written down in my journal,"},{"start":647.2,"text":"I like to dive in to my work."},{"start":647.8,"text":"But what am I working on?"},{"start":648.4,"text":"Well,"},{"start":649,"text":"I'm actually talking to myself."},{"start":649.6,"text":"I'm currently chatting with JI, who is"},{"start":650.2,"text":"an AI version of me who sounds exactly"},{"start":650.8,"text":"like me."},{"start":651.4,"text":"And I'm talking with him to improve how"},{"start":652,"text":"he sounds, to make his accent sound even"},{"start":652.6,"text":"more like mine. Recently, I also"},{"start":653.2,"text":"improved how JI gives you feedback in"},{"start":653.8,"text":"even more detail."},{"start":654.4,"text":"Finally, I built a role-play exercise so"},{"start":655,"text":"that you can practice speaking in any"},{"start":655.6,"text":"scenario that you want. In a cafe, at a"},{"start":656.2,"text":"job interview, or any custom scenario"},{"start":656.8,"text":"that you choose."},{"start":657.4,"text":"Hey Jay, what does it mean when people"},{"start":658,"text":"say it's just gone 12?"},{"start":658.6,"text":"When people say it's just gone"},{"start":720,"text":", it"},{"start":720.6,"text":"means it's a little bit past"},{"start":721.2,"text":"."},{"start":721.8,"text":"Now, I've finished working on Sprout,"},{"start":722.4,"text":"and the time is"},{"start":723,"text":"."},{"start":723.6,"text":"It's coming up to"},{"start":724.2,"text":". It's getting on"},{"start":724.8,"text":"for"},{"start":725.4,"text":". It's almost"},{"start":726,"text":"."},{"start":726.6,"text":"We call"},{"start":727.2,"text":"noon or midday."},{"start":727.8,"text":"Midday is more conversational."},{"start":728.4,"text":"And at midday, I like to do my favorite"},{"start":729,"text":"thing."},{"start":729.6,"text":"Nighty nighty."},{"start":730.2,"text":"Ah."},{"start":730.8,"text":"Nap."},{"start":731.4,"text":"Other ways to say nap are to have a kip."},{"start":732,"text":"Kip is very British, and it can be a"},{"start":732.6,"text":"verb or a noun."},{"start":733.2,"text":"You can kip, or you can have a kip."},{"start":733.8,"text":"You can also say a cat nap or a power"},{"start":734.4,"text":"nap, which both mean a quick nap."},{"start":735,"text":"What day is it?"},{"start":735.6,"text":"What date is it?"},{"start":736.2,"text":"This is a calendar."},{"start":736.8,"text":"These are the days. Sunday, Monday,"},{"start":737.4,"text":"Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday,"},{"start":738,"text":"Saturday. And these are the dates. The"},{"start":738.6,"text":"1st, the 2nd, the 3rd,"},{"start":739.2,"text":"and the 4th of April."},{"start":739.8,"text":"Day and date sounds"},{"start":740.4,"text":"very similar. So, let's make sure that"},{"start":741,"text":"we don't confuse them."},{"start":741.6,"text":"Hey Jay, what day is it today?"},{"start":742.2,"text":"Today, it's Saturday, Mario."},{"start":742.8,"text":"It's the weekend."},{"start":743.4,"text":"It's the 25th"},{"start":744,"text":"of April."},{"start":744.6,"text":"And remember, Mario,"},{"start":745.2,"text":"and you,"},{"start":745.8,"text":"we don't say the 25 of April, we say the"},{"start":746.4,"text":"25th."},{"start":747,"text":"The 25th."},{"start":747.6,"text":"Got it?"},{"start":748.2,"text":"Good."},{"start":748.8,"text":"And if you look at the calendar,"},{"start":749.4,"text":"you can see that day one is the first,"},{"start":750,"text":"day two is the second,"},{"start":750.6,"text":"and day three"},{"start":751.2,"text":"is the third."},{"start":751.8,"text":"So, if we say the first, do we say the"},{"start":752.4,"text":"11th?"},{"start":753,"text":"No."},{"start":753.6,"text":"It's the 11th, 12th, and 13th."},{"start":754.2,"text":"English"},{"start":754.8,"text":"is weird."},{"start":755.4,"text":"Speaking of weird, we're not as weird as"},{"start":756,"text":"those Americans who put the month first."},{"start":756.6,"text":"In England, we write the day,"},{"start":757.2,"text":"the month,"},{"start":757.8,"text":"and then the year."},{"start":758.4,"text":"Now,"},{"start":759,"text":"I have a question for you guys."},{"start":759.6,"text":"If your phone"},{"start":760.2,"text":"died"},{"start":760.8,"text":"for an entire day,"},{"start":761.4,"text":"how would you spend your time?"},{"start":762,"text":"And why?"},{"start":762.6,"text":"Would it be a good thing"},{"start":763.2,"text":"or a bad thing?"},{"start":763.8,"text":"Let me know in the comments, and let's"},{"start":764.4,"text":"start a conversation with each other."},{"start":765,"text":"Now, it's time for some trendy British"},{"start":765.6,"text":"slang."},{"start":766.2,"text":"Here are five of my favorite slang words"},{"start":766.8,"text":"in British English. And the first one is"},{"start":767.4,"text":"to faff."},{"start":768,"text":"To faff about, to faff on, or to faff"},{"start":768.6,"text":"around. And this means to waste time."},{"start":769.2,"text":"Here's an example."},{"start":769.8,"text":"John,"},{"start":770.4,"text":"stop faffing. Flight's in 2 hours."},{"start":771,"text":"Chop, chop."},{"start":771.6,"text":"The next slang word is to crack on."},{"start":772.2,"text":"Crack on."},{"start":772.8,"text":"Which means hurry up."},{"start":773.4,"text":"Here's another example."},{"start":774,"text":"We're still late."},{"start":774.6,"text":"Crack on."},{"start":775.2,"text":"Thank you."},{"start":775.8,"text":"The next slang word is"},{"start":776.4,"text":"stupid o'clock."},{"start":777,"text":"Stupid o'clock means extremely early or"},{"start":777.6,"text":"extremely late. An inconvenient time."},{"start":778.2,"text":"Here's an example."},{"start":778.8,"text":"You look knackered. Uh, Luigi."},{"start":779.4,"text":"I was up until stupid o'clock last"},{"start":780,"text":"night."},{"start":780.6,"text":"The next slang word is yonks."},{"start":781.2,"text":"We can also say donkey's years. And"},{"start":781.8,"text":"these mean a very, very, very long time."},{"start":782.4,"text":"Here's an example. Monopoly."},{"start":783,"text":"It's been yonks since we played this."},{"start":783.6,"text":"Should we play?"},{"start":784.2,"text":"Slang word number five is now and then."},{"start":784.8,"text":"Now and then means"},{"start":785.4,"text":"occasionally."},{"start":786,"text":"Here's an example."},{"start":786.6,"text":"I usually have coffee at home, but"},{"start":787.2,"text":"now and then I like to enjoy it"},{"start":787.8,"text":"in the sun in a cafe."},{"start":788.4,"text":"Now, it's time for you to practice what"},{"start":789,"text":"you learned in this video by talking to"},{"start":789.6,"text":"JI."},{"start":790.2,"text":"JI sounds exactly like me. He will ask"},{"start":790.8,"text":"you questions,"},{"start":791.4,"text":"give you feedback, and help you"},{"start":792,"text":"reinforce everything that you learned in"},{"start":792.6,"text":"this video."},{"start":793.2,"text":"Just click the link in the description"},{"start":793.8,"text":"and sign up for 7 days free."},{"start":794.4,"text":"Time is our most valuable asset."},{"start":795,"text":"We can waste it"},{"start":795.6,"text":"or use it wisely."}]}